※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4527

※ An argument that names its parameter names one the function has.  A name
※ that is not one of them is nearly always a spelling, and the parameters are
※ where to look for the right one.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8 = plus(.nope ← 1u8)
    0u6

fn plus(n: u8 ← 1u8) → u8:
    n
